            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "fur obtained from the legs of animals, especially kids, goats or sheep, and used for trimming outer garments (Veale 217) | fur obtained from the legs of animals, esp. kids, goats or sheep, and used for trimming outer garments (OED s.v. shank 2) | furs made of the skins from the legs of the animal and used for trimming outer garments (Veale 217) | [fox] fur of the leg of the fox | fur obtained from the legs of animals, esp. kids, goats or sheep, and used for trimming outer garments (Veale 217; OED s.v. shank n. 2) | fur obtained from the legs of animals, especially kids, goats or sheep, and used for trimming outer garments (Veale 217; OED s.v. shank n. 2) | shanks are fur obtained from the legs of animals, especially kids, goats or sheep, and used for trimming outer garments (Veale 217; OED s.v. shank n. 2), while a tavelyn is a small package of skins or furs, but it is unknown what they designate when used together" ;
